elate to abby  because she films abby in a lot of  close-up shots  medium shots where a lot of times when  we see harper  until the end of the film she's shot  further away we're supposed to distance  from her because as the movie goes on  they're distancing from each other and  what makes the writing about this  so effective not just in setup and how  quickly they get to the conflict here  and keep it  everything moving every scene in this  film  serves what the film is trying to say  and there's really two big things this  film's really hitting on  it's really shown in aubry plaza's line  when she says  to kristen stewart the thing i can  relate to is being in love with someone  who is afraid to show the world who they  are  that's what this movie's showing you is  this type of relationship between abby  and harper  and that abby you're sympathizing with  because  you feel for her that harper is keeping  her hidden but where it twists you is  then we get  dan levy's great monologue to avi later  on  when he's talking about how it was  easier situation for you to come out but  not everyone has that  blessing where their families totally  understanding  and it gives you that lesson with the  film about  it's not even about you your partner not  coming out right away or in a difficult  situation of judgment like this  it's about them and what they also you  have to sympathize what they're going  through so the  movie really shows you that it's  important to be who you are and brave  and come out with it but it also shows  you the effects  on both partners and how if you're the  one not in that  situation there's got to be some  understanding there of how hard that  situation that is but  on harper's end her to have to  understand how that also affects your  partner because you're trapping them and  they feel completely distanced and  closed off which just film effectively  shows and how  complicated relationships like this can  get in this situation and  with writing the best writing comes in  when you're writing these characters  lives you're in the middle of the most  chaotic situation in their life and if  you were to look at a story  of this relationship as their life goes  on this  hands down would be the most chaotic  when they first meet the family with  this big secret  and they're learning so much about each  other leading to great character growth  with harper  and abby where abby's character growth  is serving the message of the film  because  she comes around to understand harper's  situation and be sympathetic  where harper's character growth is that  she finally comes around to being  honest and being who she really is to  her family and to  not be afraid to share who she is in  love with so it checks off all the marks  there  thematically and it really works so well  now when we're talking about comedy here  what impressed me so much is to me  comedy has really struggled in film  since  early 2000s i think it's mostly been  horrible and i haven't laughed at much  stuff  but i don't remember the last time i  laughed so much  in a movie and why i applaud the writing  comedically for this film is that it  doesn't let you  go it just keeps whipping out the jokes  and they're all landing you see a  problem a lot of comedies now is they're  not whipping out enough jokes or they're  whipping a lot of jokes out  and a lot of them aren't landing and  they're just leaving it there and not  trying to make it better  this film has so much subtle humor that  goes on  even some of the jokes have multiple  layers to it you have to catch little  mannerisms when things are hinting at  it's so well done and it lets the  performances shine i think what was the  most enjoyable thing about watching a  movie like this  and is why you have to applaud clay  duval's directing is that  it's this big ensemble cast with all  these big names and you always get  worried because the history of that  with movies especially christmas ones  they 