 like when they all go out to dinner in  the beginning  first time abby's with the family and  then they bring her out this small chair  and then mackenzie dave was like you  sure it's okay she's like yeah it's just  hysterical visually  seeing her sit in that chair with  everybody and being that this movie is  about an hour 40 minutes  it times out well where you're getting  to me an hour of like  insanely funny comedy and then you get  the payoff thematically and that's where  it hits hard and everyone's gonna be  crying especially assuming harper's  coming out and it's so earned but  it gives you everything you need in a  christmas movie for it to be successful  and what people are looking for in this  type of film and what i'm talking about  it successfully gives even the side  characters growth they all  follow again simple but timely great  writing rules of  every character starts somewhere but the  end of the film they get somewhere else  there's character growth it's one pole  to another  and this comes in this final scene it  may ripe up  really fast and i think i could see the  criticism there but i think it's one of  the only  certain ways you can pull it off in the  time frame of how long the movie is  without getting maybe dragged out which  i'd rather take  not dragged out than kind of feeling a  little rush at the end with certain  characters but again because they're  minor characters so i don't feel  cheated and you get that with the  parents them coming around and how they  raise their kids and what was wrong with  it and you get that with the sisters  and you even get it really funny how  even jane  my favorite character in this film and i  thought mary holland stole the show  when she gets her line i don't have any  secrets but i'm an ally was hysterical  but the point of her always feeling  left out of everything and not taken  seriously it all hit even sloan with  allison brie who  really shows her range here she was  great i didn't even know s